WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.735
-Our next guest
is an Emmy-nominated actor

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:05.071
you know from his work
on HBO's "Silicon Valley."

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.773
He stars in the CBS sitcom
"B Positive."

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:10.043
The season-two finale
airs March 10th.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.444
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:13.779
-Knock knock.
-Don't answer.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.448
-Who's there?
-Nobody home.

00:00:16.448 --> 00:00:18.551
-Juneau.
-I'm great at these.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.119
Juneau who?

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.488
-Did you know [Juneau]
I'm headed to Alaska?

00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:23.622
-Oh!

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:26.492
-"Did you know
I'm headed to Alaska" who?

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:29.095
-Uh, no, no, no.
I'm going to Alaska.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.230
I finally decided
on my next adventure.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.466
-Why is that funny?

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.634
-I might try to work
on a fishing boat

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.638
after, you know, I spend a few
weeks exploring the wilderness,

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.573
just me and nature
in an epic battle for survival.

00:00:41.573 --> 00:00:43.877
-My money's on nature.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.412
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.513
our friend Thomas Middleditch,
everyone!

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:49.015
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:59.025 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:01.427 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:01.427 --> 00:01:05.297
Well, it is just
so nice to have you here,

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:07.900
and I feel as though
this might be

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.469
a television debut
of a new hairstyle.

00:01:10.469 --> 00:01:13.339
-Well, you know...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.541
...it's the cut
that everybody's talking about.

00:01:15.541 --> 00:01:18.043
-Yeah.
I heard you had a new one,

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.511
and I will admit,
when you first walked out,

00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:21.880
I didn't really see it.
It wasn't until I got you

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:24.250
on this angle, as you went...
-Yeah, that looks like

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.520
a pretty normal haircut.
"Oh, what's that?" you say?

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.689
"It's a braided rat tail
at the back?"

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:35.127
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.127 --> 00:01:37.397
-I mean --
-And I want to say,

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.299
this is real.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:43.202
This isn't some ha-ha funny
for-jokes extension.

00:01:43.202 --> 00:01:44.838
This is my life now.
-Yeah.

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:46.539
[ Laughter ]
This isn't one of those

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:50.410
phony Hollywood rat tails
you get on Sunset Boulevard.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:52.579
-Those are a dime a dozen,
my friend.

00:01:52.579 --> 00:01:56.448
-I mean, that must have taken,
what, a half a week to grow?

00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:57.717
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.717 --> 00:02:00.285
It's a little short now...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.285 --> 00:02:02.689
...but this baby's gonna
get down to my butt, hopefully.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.256
-Wow!
-I can whip it around, like...

00:02:04.256 --> 00:02:07.227
-This is such a big life change.
-Yeah!

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:08.961
-What makes you take the leap
to rat tail?

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:11.965
-You know, you just --
you get some free time,

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:15.735
and, uh, things change.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:19.172
A lot of introspection,
and I come out --

00:02:19.172 --> 00:02:22.976
I emerge from my cocoon
a tailed man.

00:02:22.976 --> 00:02:25.311
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.847
-We've talked about this before,
and I feel a little --

00:02:28.847 --> 00:02:30.816
Like, I have to admit to you,
I don't really believe it

00:02:30.816 --> 00:02:33.753
when we talk about the fact
that you have a pilot's license.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:37.556
-What about me makes you not
take me seriously, Seth?

00:02:37.556 --> 00:02:39.425
[ Laughter ]
-When you go to your barber,

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:40.727
you're like, "Just remember,
you need to see it

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:43.062
under, like, a helmet.
The rat tail's gotta

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.330
be long enough."
-It's got to poke out.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.032
Any headwear, ya gotta see it.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:48.401
-But this is your --

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.804
So, again, you are using
your piloting for good.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.572
I think sometimes people
might think,

00:02:53.572 --> 00:02:56.242
"Oh, he got his pilot license,
he's out there, you know,

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:57.376
going to probably
the Fyre Festival

00:02:57.376 --> 00:02:59.379
or something like that."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:02.114
You -- This is a true thing.
You have been going,

00:03:02.114 --> 00:03:05.050
and you've been ferrying dogs
from one, like,

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:08.054
rescue to another.
-Uh...

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:10.255
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.255 --> 00:03:11.524
They're like,
"Aww, that's not what I thought

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:12.758
from the rat-tail guy."

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.027
-"I thought he was gonna
take drugs up from Mexico.

00:03:15.027 --> 00:03:16.829
What the hell?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.197
No, but there are
drugs in the dogs.

00:03:18.197 --> 00:03:19.999
Don't worry about it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.999 --> 00:03:23.102
No. No, there's an organization,
Pilots N Paws, where basically

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:26.205
they act as, like, a middleman.
So, you know,

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.007
shelters will be full
in Southern California,

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:30.576
and they need to get flown up
to places with more room

00:03:30.576 --> 00:03:32.978
or occasionally
their new forever home.

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:36.315
And it's kind of a way to be,
like, do something nice,

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:40.252
get an excuse to fly around,
and then you'll end up in, like,

00:03:40.252 --> 00:03:41.888
some random spot.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:45.758
Like, I find myself in places
like Placerville

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:48.194
or Grass Valley,
up in Northern California,

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:51.631
which are, like...I guess,
towns that were founded on,

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.766
like, the California gold rush.
-Oh!

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.736
-And they remind you of it.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.105
Every bar is like,
The Old Klondike Saloon!

00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:00.572
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.572 --> 00:04:03.943
"Have a sarsaparilla
at the Pioneers Tavern!"

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.711
[ Laughter ]
"Okay, got it.

00:04:05.711 --> 00:04:08.013
Copy that.
You like your gold."

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:09.948
-I like that I was like,

00:04:09.948 --> 00:04:12.986
"How do you even get
a rescue dog in a plane?

00:04:12.986 --> 00:04:14.220
What do they --
How do they travel?"

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:15.621
-They curl up, man.
-Look at that.

00:04:15.621 --> 00:04:17.923
Oh. Those two --
Those two were great.

00:04:17.923 --> 00:04:20.292
They were two Brittany spaniels
who had, like,

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:23.196
this neurological condition.
So when I picked them up,

00:04:23.196 --> 00:04:24.897
they were like --
I forget their names.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.766
Like, "Mitzi and Barbara,
and here they are,"

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.033
and they're like,
"Guh-guh-guh guh-guh!"

00:04:28.033 --> 00:04:30.769
[ Laughter ]
And I was like, "Oh, boy!

00:04:30.769 --> 00:04:33.305
Are they gonna settle down
when we fly?"

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:34.874
'Cause they're sitting in
the back like, "Guh-guh-guh."

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.675
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:38.811
I mean, yeah, I am laughing
at them, but it was --

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:40.613
[ Laughter ]
It's sweet.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:43.182
Sometimes those brain conditions
are hilarious.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.483
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.483 --> 00:04:46.452
-You travel with your dog,
so your dog comes, too.

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.187
-I do, yes.
Well, yeah, I travel

00:04:48.187 --> 00:04:51.124
with one of them, Potter,
and I go up high.

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:53.058
-Uh-huh.
-And when you're up high,

00:04:53.058 --> 00:04:55.160
and my plane is not pressurized,
you need oxygen.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:57.296
-So even a dog needs oxygen?
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:57.296 --> 00:04:59.065
-So is this something
you can buy,

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:00.900
or did you rig this yourself?
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.235
It would be cool if I rigged it.

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.969
I'm like,
"He's got to get air somehow!"

00:05:03.969 --> 00:05:05.971
No, you buy this.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:05:05.971 --> 00:05:09.308
And so...this is in
his little sweater,

00:05:09.308 --> 00:05:11.811
and he's got earmuffs
and his little Bane mask.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.212
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.880
I really like that one.
-Yeah.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.217
-He gets really --
And what's weird is, like,

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:21.420
when he's -- when he's
oxygen-deprived

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.756
or just getting enough,
he gets real cuddly.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:26.425
So, that's, like, him, like,
crawling on me and being like,

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:28.127
"Sleep now, master?"
"Yes."

00:05:28.127 --> 00:05:30.329
[ Laughter ]
"Go to bed now, child."

00:05:30.329 --> 00:05:31.530
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.466
-"Yes, in the morning,
you'll get more air."

00:05:34.466 --> 00:05:36.302
-"Only when I
deem it necessary."

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:37.403
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:38.671
-[ Imitating air hissing ]

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:42.074
-Yeah.
I am, I am, uh...

00:05:42.074 --> 00:05:44.476
I'm is it Michael Ironside
in "Total Recall"?

00:05:44.476 --> 00:05:45.611
I'm the bad guy
in "Total Recall."

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:47.379
-Yeah, Michael Ironside.
Nice pull.

00:05:47.379 --> 00:05:48.814
-Yeah.
-And they were impressed.

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:50.916
-Yeah, you guys --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:50.916 --> 00:05:54.654
Why aren't you up to date
on Arnold Schwarzenegger,

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:56.155
Sharon Stone,
and Michael Ironside's

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:57.756
"Total Recall"?
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.756 --> 00:05:59.892
"Screw you, Benny!"
[ Grunts ]

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:01.694
-Oh, there, see?
Now they're just coming --

00:06:01.694 --> 00:06:03.129
Now they're slowly remembering,
yeah.

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.430
-"I wish I had three hands."

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:05.764
"You're just doing fine
with two."

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:07.733
-Oh, wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:07.733 --> 00:06:10.970
-That's a spicy scene.
Now, that's a spicy scene.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.038
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.038 --> 00:06:15.474
-Just doubling down,
doubling down, doubling down.

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:18.043
-It's one of the best!
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:18.043 --> 00:06:20.446
Sorry for getting too animated
over "Total Recall."

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:21.581
I feel like everyone's like,
"Settle Down."

00:06:21.581 --> 00:06:23.315
-You flew with one of your dogs.

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:25.918
That means you have another.
That doesn't go up with you?

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:29.689
-No, I realize that her time
of traveling is done.

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.957
-An older dog.
-She's an elder.

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:35.027
She's about 15.
The fun part about her,

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:38.096
and what has been a great gift,

00:06:38.096 --> 00:06:42.501
on top of just years
of great news, globally,

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:47.073
is that she has lost
the full-functioning use

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:49.275
of her hind legs
and just rear half.

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:51.544
-Okay.
-So she has a little wheelchair

00:06:51.544 --> 00:06:52.712
that I put her in.

00:06:52.712 --> 00:06:55.247
She, like, rolls around.
-All right.

00:06:55.247 --> 00:06:57.283
-And the real cherry
on the cake...

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:59.418
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.418 --> 00:07:05.557
...is that, before bed --
and I am aware that

00:07:05.557 --> 00:07:07.292
I'm talking about this
on television...

00:07:07.292 --> 00:07:10.562
-Okay, good.
-...in order to, like,

00:07:10.562 --> 00:07:12.331
lessen the chances of me
waking up the next morning

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:16.669
with a stinky treat,
I have to --

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:23.509
as instructed by my vet --
I have to encourage a movement,

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:26.011
uh, manually.
-Okay.

00:07:26.011 --> 00:07:30.082
-So I take a little bag and I,
like, carry her to a spot,

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:35.154
I hold her up, and I, uh,
you know, um...

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:36.455
play with my dog's butthole.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:37.923
[ Laughter ]

00:07:37.923 --> 00:07:41.693
And -- And --
And I don't love it.

00:07:41.693 --> 00:07:43.328
I hate it.

00:07:43.328 --> 00:07:45.998
But I do it every night.

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:48.033
And I'm happy.

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:52.138
The reward for it
is dump in my hand.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.573
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:58.110
And I'm in my neighborhood,
like, in the dark, doing this.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.545
Like, other people walking by
are, like,

00:07:59.545 --> 00:08:00.979
walking by me like, "Jesus."

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:03.115
I'm like,
"Uh, the vet told me to!"

00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:06.585
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.585 --> 00:08:10.289
It is -- It is really --
It's a real morale booster.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:11.757
[ Laughter ]

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:12.925
-Just 'cause, your whole day,

00:08:12.925 --> 00:08:14.526
you know you've got that
waiting at the end.

00:08:14.526 --> 00:08:16.662
-I know, I got to milk
my dog later on.

00:08:16.662 --> 00:08:18.197
[ Laughter ]

00:08:18.197 --> 00:08:21.033
And it's not like the normal --
the other, Potter, it's not like

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:22.868
he's any better,
'cause, like, it's late.

00:08:22.868 --> 00:08:24.236
You know,
you just want to go to bed,

00:08:24.236 --> 00:08:25.638
and dogs are such
jerks about it.

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:27.873
They're, like,
you can tell they need to poo,

00:08:27.873 --> 00:08:30.810
but they're like, "Here? No."
[ Laughter ]

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.846
"Here? Nunh-unh."
And you're like, "I can see

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:38.116
your body ready to go, and
you're still denying me this."

00:08:38.116 --> 00:08:39.818
And then, when they do it,
you're like, "Yes!"

00:08:39.818 --> 00:08:43.489
And then you're, like,
this sad man, happy for poo.

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.091
[ Laughter ]

00:08:45.091 --> 00:08:48.460
What is your life right now?

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:52.765
And I'm so acquainted
with how poo feels now.

00:08:52.765 --> 00:08:54.767
I'm like -- I always say,
if it's dry, you're like,

00:08:54.767 --> 00:08:56.468
"There's more in there,"
and now I'm sitting there

00:08:56.468 --> 00:08:59.538
trying to get more out of her.
It's so --

00:08:59.538 --> 00:09:02.140
It's so sad.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.810
We got enough to deal with.
-Yeah!

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.446
-Anyway, I'm crushing it, man.

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:08.748
[ Laughter ]

00:09:08.748 --> 00:09:10.650
-You got the rat tail.
-I got a rat tail...

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:12.384
[ Both laugh ]
...doing poo stuff...

00:09:12.384 --> 00:09:16.188
-You're a great dog owner.
Let's not --

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:18.156
"B Positive" is a wonderful show
with a wonderful cast.

00:09:18.156 --> 00:09:20.693
You mentioned in that clip,
your character was gonna go

00:09:20.693 --> 00:09:23.228
to Juneau, Alaska,
work on a fishing boat.

00:09:23.228 --> 00:09:25.330
Now that you're a man
of the air, have you ever

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.634
thought about life on the sea,
maybe getting a fishing license

00:09:28.634 --> 00:09:31.003
or something?
-Oh, no, that's, uh,

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:34.906
far too, uh, um, bloody for me.
No, I, uh --

00:09:34.906 --> 00:09:36.675
I have actually,
only recently --

00:09:36.675 --> 00:09:40.546
When the pandemic started,
I had, um...

00:09:40.546 --> 00:09:44.817
I think I was googling --
or, YouTube'ing "squalls,"

00:09:44.817 --> 00:09:47.386
"white squalls," because there's
this Canadian folk singer

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:51.490
called Stan Rogers,
who sings, like, sea shanties.

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.894
And I was like, "Mm. I wonder
what a white squall is."

00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:57.630
And like, "Oh, wow.
That's pretty stormy."

00:09:57.630 --> 00:10:00.032
And then, YouTube,
later on, was like,

00:10:00.032 --> 00:10:02.101
"I hear you're into sailing."
And I'm like,

00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:04.203
"Not really,
but what do you got, YouTube?"

00:10:04.203 --> 00:10:06.939
And YouTube is like,
"Well, there's this --

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:08.707
there's this channel,
these, like --

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:10.943
They're both so pretty.

00:10:10.943 --> 00:10:12.878
There's this, like,
pretty Australian couple,

00:10:12.878 --> 00:10:16.548
the man and a woman, who have
detached themselves from life.

00:10:16.548 --> 00:10:19.384
They sail around the world,
sailing the Vagabond.

00:10:19.384 --> 00:10:21.820
I'll give you a shout-out!
Why not?

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.021
I bought their merch.

00:10:23.021 --> 00:10:26.325
I'm weirdly obsessed
with sailing now.

00:10:26.325 --> 00:10:30.228
And, uh, yeah, they live at sea,
and I have thought about

00:10:30.228 --> 00:10:33.766
just like, "You know what?
That's it for me, boys."

00:10:33.766 --> 00:10:35.101
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.101 --> 00:10:38.571
Like, "I'll take to the seas
from now on."

00:10:38.571 --> 00:10:41.106
But I have a feeling, like,
I don't know, a week in,

00:10:41.106 --> 00:10:42.875
I would just be like,
"I want my Xbox.

00:10:42.875 --> 00:10:44.342
What am I doing?"
-Yeah.

00:10:44.342 --> 00:10:46.746
-"What am I doing?"
-"I can't believe I'm on a boat

00:10:46.746 --> 00:10:48.480
with a dog that can't [bleep]
on his own."

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:50.482
[ Laughter ]
-In a white squall.

00:10:50.482 --> 00:10:53.051
"Come on, Meatloaf!"
[ Laughter ]

00:10:53.051 --> 00:10:55.053
"Give me the goods, baby,
give me that brown gold!"

00:10:55.053 --> 00:10:57.523
-Is his name Meatloaf?
-Her name is Meatloaf!

00:10:57.523 --> 00:10:59.424
Don't mis-gender my dog!
[ Laughter ]

00:10:59.424 --> 00:11:02.127
-Oh, God.
-It's 2022.

00:11:02.127 --> 00:11:04.396
Please don't mis-gender
my dog, Seth!

00:11:04.396 --> 00:11:06.399
[ Laughter ]

00:11:06.399 --> 00:11:09.267
I'm begging you.
-All right, I hear you!

00:11:09.267 --> 00:11:11.069
Apologies to Meatloaf.

00:11:11.069 --> 00:11:13.305
She sounds wonderful.
-Yes.

00:11:13.305 --> 00:11:14.906
-This is Thomas Middleditch,
everybody.

00:11:14.906 --> 00:11:16.008
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:11:16.008 --> 00:11:17.109
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:18.744
-The season-two finale
of "B Positive"

00:11:18.744 --> 00:11:20.246
airs March 10th on CBS.

